            "b": 0.5411764705882353,
            "a": 0.8
          },
          "text": "A waffle plot displays categorical data as colored rectangles on a grid. Each grid unit represents a proportional ratio of the total data count. A waffle plot is often used to visualize proportions or percentages. ",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontColor": {
            "r": 0.15294117647058825,
            "g": 0.15294117647058825,
            "b": 0.16470588235294117,
            "a": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "eafLAi38any:4",
          "type": "STICKY",
          "x": 400,
          "y": 120,
          "width": 360,
          "height": 50,
          "backgroundColor": {
            "r": 0.9921568627450981,
            "g": 0.9019607843137255,
            "b": 0.5411764705882353,
            "a": 0.8
          },
          "text": "Load data from an online source. ",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontColor": {
            "r": 0.15294117647058825,
            "g": 0.15294117647058825,
            "b": 0.16470588235294117,
            "a": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "eafLAi38any:5",
          "type": "STICKY",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 460,
          "width": 710,
          "height": 40,
          "backgroundColor": {
            "r": 0.03137254901960784,
            "g": 0.1843137254901961,
            "b": 0.28627450980392155,
            "a": 0.8
          },
          "text": "A waffle plot is a complex plot which displays calculated grid data instead of the original input data. Behind the scenes, a separate grid table is generated, and the X- and Y-positions represent grid indexes instead of data attributes.",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontColor": {
            "r": 0.9333333333333333,
            "g": 0.9333333333333333,
            "b": 0.9333333333333333,
            "a": 1
          }
        },
        {
